※ pl4g-test: compile=ok run=native,qemu exit=0 diag=none

※ A division answers with a result, so one whose operands are both written
※ down and have no answer between them is well formed: its value is the error.
※ It is still worth saying, since the error is the only thing such a division
※ will ever produce -- so both cases are warnings rather than errors, and
※ `@[expect]` here both means them and asserts the compiler noticed.

@[visible]
let kept: mut u8 = 0u8

@[startup]
fn main() → u8:
    @[expect(4215)]
    kept ← 100u8 ÷ 0u8 ?? 1u8
    @[expect(4215)]
    kept ← 100u8 % 0u8 ?? 2u8
    @[expect(4223), ignore(5005)]
    ⁻128i8 ÷ ⁻1i8 ?? ⁻3i8
    0u8
